{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Hear, O Israel.</b> Since this is the end intended by the blessed El for you in His abundant lovingkindness, it is fitting that you hear and understand the intent of the blessed El in all these things." "<b>And keep to do what is good for you.</b> And you should strive to do then, out of love, to find favor before Him, that which is good for you to acquire eternal felicity; and likewise you shall keep to do, you whose numbers shall greatly increase — and this is through keeping righteousness and justice for His honor." "<b>As HaShem, the Elohim of your fathers, spoke to you — a land flowing with milk and honey.</b> As He spoke to you — a land flowing with milk and honey, prepared for those who serve Him for this end: that you may be sustained in it without distress, and have leisure for study and for practice, to be fruitful and to multiply."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:41.607763923Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}